    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0098" n="56" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg56"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 293.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 8, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In conformity with the directions contained
                    in your despatch No. 429, of the 20th of December, 1862, I have transmitted to
                    Earl Russell the copies of memorials and other papers relating to the
                    destruction by the vessel No 290 of the ships Virginia, Benjamin Tucker, Elisha
                    Dunbar, Ocean Rover, Altamaha, and Ocmulgee, which were sent to me with that
                    despatch.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d27-a1.xml" xpointer="d27-a1"/>
            </div>
